===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|approche|t=approach, arrival}}, from {{m|enm|approchen}}, {{m|enm|aprochen|t=to come or go near, approach; to adjoin, be close by; to enter (someone’s) presence; to be or become involved; to reach (a certain state); to arrive; to befall, happen to; to become similar to, resemble; to be a match for (someone)}}; see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]].<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=apprōche|pos=n|id=MED1991}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=9837|date=July 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|also|figuratively}} An [[act#Noun|act]] of [[draw#Verb|drawing]] [[near#Adverb|near]] in [[place#Noun|place]] or [[time#Noun|time]]; an [[advancing#Noun|advancing]] or [[coming#Noun|coming]] near.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|act=III|scene=iii|page=136|column=2|passage=Ah, what a ſigne it is of euill life, <br> Where death's '''approach''' is ſeene ſo terrible.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Love's Labour's Lost Q1|act=II|scene=i|page=15|lines=81–84|passage=''Nauar'' had notice of your faire '''approch'''. <br> And he and his compettitours in [[oath|oth]], <br> Were all addreſt to meete you gentle Lady <br> Before I came: {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Defoe Crusoe|page=353|passage=Theſe Things, and the '''Approach''' of Night, called us off, or elſe, as ''Friday'' would have had us, we ſhould certainly have taken the Skin of this monſtrous Creature off, which was worth ſaving; but we had near three Leagues to go, and our Guide haſten'd us; ſo we left him, and went forward on our Journey.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Dunciad|year=1729|book=3|pages=169–170|pageref=170|lines=337–338 and 345–346|passage=She comes! the Cloud-compelling pow'r, behold! <br> With night primæval, and with Chaos old. <br> {{...}} <br> Thus at her felt '''approach''', and ſecret might, <br> Art after Art goes out, and all is Night.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Samuel Horsley|chapter=Sermon I. [[w:Epistle of James|St. James]] v. 8. ''For the coming of the Lord draweth nigh.''|title=Sermons|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{...|Printed and sold by}} T. and J. Swords,{{nb...|No. 160 Pearl-Street.}}|year=1811|volume=I|page=10|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=cBs3AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA10|oclc=5327685|passage=The '''approach''' of summer, says our Lord, is not more surely indicated by the first appearances of spring, than the final destruction of the wicked by the beginnings of vengeance on this impenitent people.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|page=6|passage="A merry Christmas, uncle! God save you!" cried a cheerful voice. It was the voice of Scrooge's nephew, who came upon him so quickly that this was the first intimation he had of his '''approach.'''}}
#* {{RQ:Eliot Adam Bede|volume=I|chapter=The Hall Farm|page=130|passage=There is quite a concert of noises: the great bull-dog, chained against the stables, is thrown into furious exasperation by the unwary '''approach''' of a cock too near the mouth of his kennel, and sends forth a thundering bark, which is answered by two fox-hounds shut up in the opposite cow-house; {{...}}}}
# An act of coming near in [[character]] or [[value#Noun|value]]; an [[approximation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Richard Owen|chapter=Appendix B. On the Orang, Chimpanzee, and Gorilla, with Reference to the ‘Transmutation of Species.’|title=On the Classification and Geographical Distribution of the Mammalia,{{nb...|Being the Lecture on Sir Robert Reade’s Foundation, Delivered before the University of Cambridge, in the Senate-House, May 10, 1859. To which is Added an Appendix “On the Gorilla,” and “On the Extinction and Transmutation of Species.”}}|location=London|publisher=[[w:John William Parker|John W[illiam] Parker and Son]],{{nb...|West Strand.}}|date=10 May 1859|page=85|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=WhuzAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA85|oclc=926205528|passage=The canine, judging from the figures published by M. [[w:Édouard Lartet|[Édouard] Lartet]], seems to be less developed than in the male chimpanzees, gorillas and orang. In which character the fossil, if it belonged to a male, makes a nearer '''approach''' to the human type; but it is one which many of the inferior monkeys also exhibit, and is by no means to be trusted as significant of true affinity, supposing even the sex of the fossil to be known as being male.}}
# {{lb|en|also|figuratively}} An [[avenue]], [[passage#Noun|passage]], or [[way#Noun|way]] by which a [[building#Noun|building]] or place can be [[approach#Verb|approached]]; an [[access#Noun|access]].
#* {{RQ:Herbert Temple|chapter=Dulnesse|page=108|passage=Where are my lines then? my '''approaches'''? views? <br> Where are my window-ſongs?}}
#* {{RQ:Cowper Homer|volume=II|book=VII|page=151|lines=100–102 and 109–112|passage={{...}} he ſaw <br> As of the ſun or moon illuming clear <br> The palace of Phæacia's mighty King. <br> {{...}} <br> Maſtiffs, in gold and ſilver, lined the '''approach''' <br> On either ſide, by art celeſtial framed <br> Of [[w:Vulcan (mythology)|Vulcan]], guardian of [[w:Alcinous|Alcinoüs]] gate <br> For ever, unobnoxious to decay.}}
## {{lb|en|climbing}} A [[path#Noun|path]] [[take#Verb|taken]] to [[reach#Verb|reach]] the [[climbing#Noun|climbing]] [[area]], for example, from a [[car park]], [[road#Noun|road]], etc.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A [[manner]] of [[make#Verb|making]] (a [[policy]]) or [[solve#Verb|solving]] (a [[problem#Noun|problem]], etc.).
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=In the Matter of Amendment of Section 64.702 of the Commission’s Rules and Regulations (Second Computer Inquiry): Final Decision|series=Docket no. 20828; FCC 80-189|journal=Federal Communications Commission Reports: Decisions and Reports of the Federal Communications Commission of the United States|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=|date=2 May 1980|year_published=1982|volume=76 (2nd Series)|section=section IV (Comments), paragraph 41|page=402|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=ien.35559002076648&view=1up&seq=1033|oclc=908804239|passage=Our proposed definitional '''approach''' to the data processing-communications dilemma evoked considerable discussion. There is uniform disagreement and confusion as to the regulatory implications of the proposed definitional terms.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=[[w:J. Skelly Wright|J[ames] Skelly Wright]], Chief Judge, {{w|United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit}}|title=Lead Industries Association, Inc., Petitioner, v. Environmental Protection Agency, Respondent (No. 78-2201)|journal=[[w:Federal Reporter|Federal Reporter{{nb...|Cases Argued and Determined in the United States Court of Appeals, United States Court of Claims, United States Court of Customs and Patent Appeals and Temporary Emergency Court of Appeals}}]]|series=2nd Series|location=St. Paul, Minn.|publisher=[[w:West (publisher)|West Publishing Co.]]|date=27 June 1980|year_published=1981|volume=647|issue=1–3|page=1136|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=uc1.b4441702&view=1up&seq=1218|column=|oclc=891573999|passage=Its [the {{w|United States Environmental Protection Agency}}'s] initial '''approach''' to controlling the amount of lead in the ambient air was to limit lead emissions from automobiles by restricting the amount of lead in gasoline.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Congressional Research Service|chapter=Article I: Legislative Power: Separation of Powers Limitations|editors=Johnny H. Killian; George A. Costello|title=[[w:Constitution of the United States|The Constitution of the United States of America]]: Analysis and Interpretation: 1988 Supplement:{{nb...|Annotations of Cases Decided by the Supreme Court of the United States to June 29, 1988}}|series=100th [[w:United States Congress|Congress]], 2nd Session, [[w:United States Senate|Senate]] Document|seriesvolume=no. 100-43; United States Congressional Serial Set; no. 13854|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|U.S. Government Printing Office]]|year=1989|page=4|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=pwYwAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA4|oclc=968505334|passage=The functional '''approach''' [to separation of powers issues] emphasizes the core functions of each branch and asks whether the challenged action threatens the essential attributes of the legislative, executive, or judicial function or functions. Under this '''approach''', there is considerable flexibility in the moving branch, usually Congress acting to make structural or institutional change, if there is little significant risk of impairment of a core function or in the case of such a risk if there is a compelling reason for the action.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} An [[opportunity]] of drawing near; [[access#Noun|access]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Essayes|chapter=Of Ambition. XXXVI.|page=221|passage=''Honour'' hath three Things in it: The Vantage Ground to doe Good: The '''approach''' to Kings and principall Persons: And the Raiſing of a Mans owne Fortunes.}}
#* {{RQ:Swift Cadenus and Vanessa|page=21|passage=The Learned met with free '''Approach''', <br> Although they came not in a Coach.}}
#* {{RQ:John Gay Fables|fablenumber=XVI|fable=The Pin and the Needle|page=1|passage=Now, rais'd again from low '''approach''', <br> She [a pin] viſits in the doctor's coach; <br> Here, there, by various fortune toſt, <br> At laſt in ''Greſham'' hall was loſt.}}
